<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="102" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Workload-placement governance — new ADR (BFF vs Azure Functions vs Container Apps Jobs), aligned amendments, all documentation aligned, ArchTest fixes, drift guard</title>
    <phase>Governance — background-work placement</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Edits ADRs, binding constraints, skills and tests/Spaarke.ArchTests (TEST-MODIFYING override).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>ADR authoring + cross-repo governance with a binding CI guard; high blast radius. The ADR draft additionally gets a Fable-tier adversarial review (owner 2026-09-12).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches .claude/ (main-session only) and skill directives (serial PRs only).</parallel-reason>
    <deps></deps>
    <tags>governance, adr, documentation, skill-directive, testing, background</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1–2 sessions</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Owner 2026-09-12, raised by task 100's review: "we do not want to prohibit use of azure functions and we want to use them where they are the right fit … yes new ADR — BUT we need to ensure that all documentation is aligned so we do not get drift"</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>The repo's directives give four incompatible answers about where timer, queue and event work belongs (no Functions; Functions only for narrow out-of-band work; timer/queue/webhook work goes to Functions; scheduled work is in-process with no Functions). The code follows none consistently. Replace them with ONE owner-approved placement policy in a new ADR, align every document to it, and add a CI guard so the old phrasings cannot return.</prompt>
  <role>Spaarke architecture steward — ADR authoring, AI-procedure maintenance, NetArchTest fitness functions.</role>
  <goal>One authoritative placement ADR; ADR-001/004/013/036 amended to point to it; every in-scope directive states the policy only by pointer; a Tier-1 ArchTest fails on reintroduced stale phrasings; the ADR-001 ArchTest's message and scan are correct.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Evaluation, owner decisions D1–D7 and all evidence: notes/decisions/workload-placement-policy-evaluation.md (read FIRST). Best-practice research with URLs: .claude/agent-memory/researcher/background-work-hosting-best-practice-2026-09-12.md. The new ADR number is ADR-052 (ADR-050 and ADR-051 exist concise-only; verify no other branch has claimed 052 before creating).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">docs/adr/ADR-052-workload-placement.md</file>
      <file role="new">.claude/adr/ADR-052-workload-placement.md</file>
      <file role="amend">docs/adr/ADR-001-minimal-api-and-workers.md + .claude/adr/ADR-001-minimal-api.md</file>
      <file role="amend">docs/adr/ADR-036-background-job-infrastructure.md + .claude/adr/ADR-036-background-job-infrastructure.md</file>
      <file role="amend">docs/adr/ADR-004-async-job-contract.md + .claude/adr/ADR-004-job-contract.md</file>
      <file role="amend">docs/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md + .claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md (decision-table row only)</file>
      <file role="amend">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/ADR001_MinimalApiTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/WorkloadPlacementDocDriftTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/SourceScan.cs + CredentialCensusTests.cs (fitness-function conventions: negative + positive controls, allowlist with reasons, maintenance procedure in the file)</file>
      <file role="procedure">.claude/skills/ai-procedure-maintenance/SKILL.md (Checklist A)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-12 D1">Scope: policy. No prohibition of Azure Functions; placement is decided per workload on merit (streamline / performance / flexibility vs. complexity).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-12 D2/D3">Scope: identity and tenancy. Functions reuse the stamp's BFF identity by default, consistent with Model 1 / Model 2; a shared multi-tenant Function is acceptable for Model 1; Model 2 is per customer.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-12 D4">Scope: tie-breaker. When neither host is clearly stronger, choose the option with fewer moving parts.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-12 D5">Scope: anti-drift. ADR-052 is the only place the placement rule is stated in full; every other document carries at most a one-line summary plus a link. A blocking ArchTest enforces it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §6.5">Scope: sequencing. Path B — the ADR changes land before the code that relies on them (tasks 103, 100).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §3">Scope: .claude/ edits. Main session only; add a .claude/CHANGELOG.md entry; follow ai-procedure-maintenance Checklist A.</constraint>
    <constraint source="tests/CLAUDE.md (ArchTests KEEP path)">Scope: fitness functions. Every new or changed rule carries a negative control (fires on a seeded violation), a positive control (does not fire on the sanctioned shape), a written reason + ADR citation per allowlist entry, and its maintenance procedure in the file.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: history. Historical records are not rewritten — ADR history/context sections, .claude/archive/**, and notes of closed projects. The drift guard allowlists them explicitly, each with a reason. Active projects' CLAUDE.md files (projects/INDEX.md) get a one-line pointer correction; archived projects are untouched.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-12">Scope: review. A Fable-tier adversarial review of the ADR-052 draft and amendments, against the evidence, before they are applied.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Read the evaluation note. Confirm ADR-052 is unclaimed (master, open PRs, other worktrees' projects).</step>
    <step order="1">Draft ADR-052 (full + concise) and the ADR-001 / ADR-036 / ADR-004 / ADR-013 amendments in notes/drafts/.</step>
    <step order="2">Fable-tier adversarial review of the drafts against notes/decisions/workload-placement-policy-evaluation.md; resolve every finding (fix, or record why not).</step>
    <step order="3">Apply the ADRs and all indexes (docs/adr/README-ADRs.md, .claude/adr/INDEX.md, ADR-VALIDATION-PROCESS.md).</step>
    <step order="4">Align every in-scope document listed in the evaluation note §4.1 (constraints, patterns, skills, architecture/standards/procedures/guides/data-model docs, PR template, project-setup template, active project CLAUDE.md pointers), correcting IJobHandler&lt;T&gt; to IJobHandler and the admin guide's Dataverse-backed claims.</step>
    <step order="5">ArchTests: fix ADR001_MinimalApiTests message and make the attribute test inspect method-level attributes; add WorkloadPlacementDocDriftTests.</step>
    <step order="6">File the over-time GitHub issues (evaluation note §5).</step>
    <step order="7">Verify: ArchTests green; negative controls fire; repo grep for the banned phrasings; CHANGELOG; notes.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the Fable review finds a material flaw in the owner-approved policy DIRECTION (not wording) — e.g. a case where D1–D4 produce an unsafe or contradictory outcome — STOP and bring it to the owner before applying anything.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>ADR-001 (host), ADR-004 (queue mechanism), ADR-036 (schedule mechanism), bff-extensions.md (checklist) — each states part of the rule, inconsistently.</existing>
    <extension>Amending ADR-001 alone was considered; rejected by the owner (D5) because provisioning, identity and future Functions projects all need one citable placement ADR, and ADR-001 is about the BFF runtime.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Agents keep receiving contradictory MUSTs: task 100 was flagged as an ADR violation for following the newest ADR; new projects are seeded with "no Azure Functions" by the project-setup template; five timer services were added after ADR-036 forbade them.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">docs/adr/ADR-052-workload-placement.md, .claude/adr/ADR-052-workload-placement.md, four amended ADRs, aligned directives</output>
    <output type="test">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/ADR001_MinimalApiTests.cs (fixed), tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/WorkloadPlacementDocDriftTests.cs (new)</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-102-workload-placement-governance.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">ADR-052 exists (full + concise) and is indexed. It states: the two-question model (host vs in-BFF mechanism); fit signals F1–F5 and stay-in-BFF signals B1–B4; the Spaarke costs; owner decisions D1–D4; the Functions guardrails; Durable Task allowed on Durable Task Scheduler, with a written reason required for hand-rolled orchestration; no new WebJobs; no user-facing BFF endpoints or user-token work in Functions.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ADR-001, ADR-004, ADR-013 and ADR-036 carry dated amendments that point to ADR-052 and do not restate the placement rule. ADR-036's amendment states the actual runtime (in-memory store, per-instance cron, non-durable disable) and the exactly-once / idempotency rules task 103 implements.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Outside allowlisted historical entries (each with a reason), in-scope surfaces contain none of the banned stale phrasings: flat "no Azure Functions" / "Functions are not permitted" / "do not use Azure Functions"; "timer/queue/webhook → Functions"; "IJobHandler&lt;T&gt;".</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">code-review, adr-check (+ its reference rules), adr-aware, task-create and design-to-spec route host → ADR-052, schedule-driven → IScheduledJob / ADR-036, and queue-driven → IJobHandler / ADR-004.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ADR001_MinimalApiTests: its message says Functions are not permitted INSIDE the BFF assembly. Its attribute test inspects method-level attributes. A negative control proves it fires on a seeded Function-attributed method; a positive control proves it does not fire on a sanctioned method.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">WorkloadPlacementDocDriftTests runs in Spaarke.ArchTests (Tier 1, blocking), per notes/drafts/drift-guard-design.draft.md: banned-phrase regexes; an allowlist by reasoned region markers (a marker without a reason fails); negative controls (each banned phrase; a reasonless marker); a positive control (the aligned tree passes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Three further ArchTests, each with negative + positive controls: (a) a ratchet — no new hand-rolled timer BackgroundService in Sprk.Bff.Api, with the existing set allow-listed with reasons and able only to shrink; (b) host-neutrality — no IScheduledJob implementation depends on ScheduledJobHost, IBackgroundJobStore or ScheduledJobRegistry; (c) Functions projects — any project referencing the Functions worker SDK lives under src/server/functions/ and does not reference Sprk.Bff.Api, and source under src/server/functions/** uses no MSAL confidential-client or managed-identity-assertion types (ConfidentialClientApplicationBuilder, ManagedIdentityClientAssertion, WithClientAssertion, AcquireTokenOnBehalfOf) — owner 2026-09-13, ADR-052 §6 identity row: a Function uses ADR-028 A4's app-only row, never its confidential-client row.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ADR-004 A1 withdraws the Durable Functions prohibition; ADR-052 §7 places Durable Task in its own host, never inside Sprk.Bff.Api, and ADR001_MinimalApiTests still bans the Durable Task namespaces in the BFF assembly.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ADR-036 A1 states in one line that, until task 103 merges, the shipped jobs rely on per-unit idempotency (owner 2026-09-12: dev only, no formal exception).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">docs/guides/BACKGROUND-JOBS-ADMIN-GUIDE.md no longer claims Dataverse-backed history, disable or de-duplication that the code does not have.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The eight over-time GitHub issues (evaluation note §5) are filed and linked from the task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A .claude/CHANGELOG.md entry exists. The full Spaarke.ArchTests suite is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Created 2026-09-12 from the task 100 review. Blocks 103 (the lease is sanctioned by ADR-036 A1 / ADR-052) and, through 103, task 100.

Fable-tier review (2026-09-12): direction D1–D7 holds and the escalation trigger did not fire; the v1 drafts were not ready. v2 fixes: the Durable contradiction (ADR-004 ban withdrawn; Durable Task never inside the BFF); the identity-reuse MECHANISM (the Function runs app-only as the managed identity — never as the BFF app registration, no OBO; SPE access keyed to the app registration is not inherited); Functions projects under src/server/functions/ so the tenant/credential ArchTests cover Model 1 shared apps; the ADR-036 lease text no longer pre-empts task 103's Redis escalation; the retry/idempotency rules defined per unit (atomic claim before the side effect, completion marker after); "one dispatch per schedule", not "exactly once"; queue consumers are never "long-lived listeners"; "when next touched" defined; fleet-scoped tenancy and Durable Task Scheduler tenancy; owner-approval points; a transitional path-A exception.

ADDITIONAL documents to align (review list b), beyond evaluation note §4.1: ADR-004 (concise L31, full L75); .claude/constraints/api.md L61–69, ai.md L67, plugins.md L99, jobs.md L29/50/110/135; ADR-002 (concise L60, full L80); ADR-032 (full L242); ADR-013 full L407; .claude/skills/code-review/references/review-checklist.md L94–104; .claude/skills/adr-check/references/adr-validation-rules.md L10/16/21–28/41/500; .claude/skills/adr-aware/SKILL.md L150; .coderabbit.yaml; src/server/shared/Spaarke.Scheduling/ScheduledJobHost.cs L28 (comment); docs/guides/RAG-ARCHITECTURE.md L824; docs/architecture/INSIGHTS-ENGINE-ARCHITECTURE.md; infra/insights/modules/function-app.bicep (header note: pre-ADR-052 — its per-tenant UAMI and allowSharedKeyAccess:true must be aligned before first use; GitHub issue); knowledge/azure-functions-isv/README.md (a pointer note); docs/guides/SPAARKE-CUSTOMER-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md §8 (scan roots include src/server/functions) and SPAARKE-SPE-CONTAINER-TYPE-TOPOLOGY.md §3A (a Function reusing the managed identity inherits its app-only SPE access; only a dedicated identity needs its own grant).

COMPLETED 2026-09-13 (session 10). Record: notes/task-102-workload-placement-governance.md. Owner approved the v2 drafts and chose the identity wording "consistent with the existing approach": a Function reuses the stamp UAMI app-only (ADR-028 A4 app-only row); CIAM Graph and Power BI clients are not inherited; confidential-client / credential / OBO / Dataverse-impersonation types are banned under src/server/functions/** by ArchTest. ADR-052 Accepted. Step 9.5: code-review (no Critical) and adr-check (pass with fixes) — every fix applied. ArchTests 288/288; drift scan clean; src/server edits comment-only. Follow-ups #976–#986. Non-blocking owner decisions carried: not-started POMLs in active projects still carry the old flat ban; confirm the impersonation MUST NOT; Insights D-20.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
